  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kenya, Zimbabwe, Tanzania. The project works towards strengthening entrepreneurship, leadership, and advocacy skills among youth with disabilities. Youth living with physical and/or intellectual disabilities being involved in decision making process, policy making and to participate in cultural activities, income generating projects and food security. The project will strive to address the challenge of limited Freedom of Movement amongst Youth with Disabilities through organised international youth conventions and inter-country learning exchange programs. The Participants will engage in cultural exchange activities, learn new sports, art, music, and other cultural practices during their period of enrolment.</narrative>
  </description>
